cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "What the Pit Wall Knew: judging Ferrari's 2022 strategy calls using only what was known at the time"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Mohapatra
    given-names: Muktanan
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-31
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/tinySage/what-the-pit-wall-knew"
abstract: >-
  A Bayesian lap-time model and a whole-field race simulator, refitted at each
  decision lap on the data available then, used to judge three of Ferrari's
  2022 strategy calls (Hungary, Silverstone, Monaco) against a verdict rule
  committed before any results.
keywords:
  - Formula 1
  - race strategy
  - Bayesian modelling
  - Monte Carlo simulation
  - FastF1
